{"study_accession":"PRJNA494706","secondary_study_accession":"SRP163470","title":"RNAseq of CD8+ and CD8- MAIT cells in human peripheral blood","description":"Mucosa-associated invariant T (MAIT) cells are unconventional innate-like T cells that recognize microbial riboflavin metabolites presented by the MHC class I-like protein MR1. Human MAIT cells predominantly express the CD8α co-receptor (CD8+), with a smaller subset lacking both CD4 and CD8 (DN). However, it is unclear if these two MAIT cell sub-populations distinguished by CD8α represent functionally distinct subsets. To address this, we investigated the phenotypic, transcriptional, and functional differences between CD8+ and DN MAIT cells using human samples from peripheral blood, mucosal tissues, and fetal tissues. Overall design: We FACS sorted CD8+ and CD8- MAIT cells from human peripheral blood and performed bulk RNAseq on these cells","pubmed":"30442667","geo_series":"","n_samples":8,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN10177547","study_accession":"PRJNA494706","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"ND434-MAIT-CD8pos","description":"ND434-MAIT-CD8pos","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3417031","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2019-01-03","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","Mucosa-associated invariant T (MAIT) cells"],["cell markers","CD8+"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR7965716","experiment_accession":"SRX4799339","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":21183908,"base_count":3056537403,"first_public":"2019-01-03","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM3417031: ND434-MAIT-CD8pos Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN10177548","study_accession":"PRJNA494706","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"ND434-MAIT-CD8neg","description":"ND434-MAIT-CD8neg","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3417030","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"20